{
  "_comment": "FortiGate lab web-filter / AV test target list. 'expect' (block|allow|mixed) is a reporting hint. 'weight' is relative hit frequency (higher = hit more often; normal traffic is weighted up). Toggle a category with \"enabled\": false. Edit freely for your lab.",

  "_source_ips_comment": "Local source IPs to bind outgoing traffic to (round-robin), so each appears as a separate client on the FortiGate. Must already be assigned to a NIC on this machine. Empty list = OS default. Override at runtime with --source-ips.",
  "source_ips": [
    "10.21.1.10",
    "10.21.1.12",
    "10.21.1.15",
    "10.21.1.20",
    "10.21.1.32",
    "10.21.1.41"
  ],

  "_threat_feeds_comment": "Pull the same external threat-feed lists the FortiGate uses and mix a small random assortment into traffic to prove the feeds are matching. Real malicious indicators - feed targets are never fully downloaded or saved. mix_rate 0.025 = ~2.5% of connections. Set enabled=false to skip.",
  "threat_feeds": {
    "enabled": true,
    "mix_rate": 0.025,
    "poll_interval_sec": 600,
    "max_per_pass": 40,
    "fetch_timeout_sec": 20,
    "feeds": {
      "urls": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bbartik/threat-feed-examples/refs/heads/main/bad-urls.txt",
